{"title":"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the sides of a triangle have lengths 2, 3, and 4, what is the radius of the circle circumscribing the triangle?\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad39e455fe156ef0c687ce7c7d910ebd4f9c9f27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 8/\\sqrt{15}  \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 5/2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\sqrt{6} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ }  (\\sqrt{6} + 1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"499\" height=\"24\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>One simple solution is using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> formulas: by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Heron%27s_formula\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Heron&#39;s formula\">Heron's formula</a>, a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> with sides of length 2, 3 and 4 has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c1340db188fba4cc90d120fa2540cd2612029d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac92 \\cdot \\frac 52 \\cdot \\frac 32 \\cdot \\frac 12} = \\frac34 \\sqrt{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"180\" height=\"43\" />.  But it also has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9160f12e9d95c42d8f4be7d32083cbcf5d56bc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{abc}{4R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"38\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumradius\" title=\"Circumradius\">circumradius</a>) so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d2769adf5a1aec962538da1d75d459ae989eea7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\frac{2\\cdot3\\cdot4}{4 (\\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{15})} = \\frac{6\\cdot\\frac{4}{3}}{\\sqrt{15}} = \\frac8{\\sqrt{15}} \\Longrightarrow \\mathrm{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"301\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Alternatively, let <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex\" title=\"Vertex\">vertex</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be opposide the side of length 2.  Then by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc98a0fff7a7486d7782320427fa4377c888d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2 = 3^2 + 4^2 - 2\\cdot3\\cdot4\\cos A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"215\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56243301a7596c547512b684490fac49ed1db48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos A = \\frac{3^2 + 4^2 - 2^2}{2\\cdot3\\cdot 4} = \\frac78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"199\" height=\"39\" />.  Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/9409d68e41fc8f0cb280300ca291be382acf4727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin A = \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac78\\right)^2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"219\" height=\"53\" />.  Then by the extended <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/7/2873f2b0160155f836afc58482f59e88ace263ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\frac12 \\frac a{\\sin A} = \\frac12 \\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{15}/8} = \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{15}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"260\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_28\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 28\">Previous Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_30\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 30\">Next Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam\">Back to Exam</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018000350\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 55/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2341/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3433:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018000350 and revision id 48162. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}